      {
        "type": "Interpretation",
        "id": "I1",
        "study_id": "S1",
        "part_id": null,
        "statement": "The multistep process produced a comprehensible and conceptually equivalent EQ-5D-Y-5L Bahasa Indonesia for children aged 8 to 16.",
        "finding_ids": [
          "F1",
          "F3",
          "F6",
          "F7"
        ],
        "source": [
          "scale/protocol-2.0/fulltext-preparation-v2/markdown/Pf53a5ee15eef.md"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Interpretation",
        "id": "I2",
        "study_id": "S1",
        "part_id": null,
        "statement": "The qualifiers of the existing EQ-5D-3L and EQ-5D-Y-3L Bahasa Indonesia should be amended to restore parallel wording across EQ-5D versions, and results from these two measures should be interpreted with caution in international comparisons until then; the amendment is timely because no national Indonesian 3L value set yet exists.",
        "finding_ids": [
          "F2",
          "F4"
        ],
        "source": [
          "scale/protocol-2.0/fulltext-preparation-v2/markdown/Pf53a5ee15eef.md"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Interpretation",
        "id": "I3",
        "study_id": "S1",
        "part_id": null,
        "statement": "Difficulty in discriminating between levels 2 and 3 is not specific to Bahasa Indonesia and has been reported in Chichewa and Chinese, so linguistic experts should refine in-between qualifiers and valuation practice sessions should explain the qualifier rank order.",
        "finding_ids": [
          "F5"
        ],
        "source": [
          "scale/protocol-2.0/fulltext-preparation-v2/markdown/Pf53a5ee15eef.md"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Interpretation",
        "id": "I4",
        "study_id": "S1",
        "part_id": null,
        "statement": "The example-giving section of cognitive debriefing is cognitively demanding for children and could be replaced by the ranking exercise developed for EQ-5D youth translations; forward translation guidance should also request simple fluent child-appropriate drafts alongside literal ones.",
        "finding_ids": [
          "F7"
        ],
        "source": [
          "scale/protocol-2.0/fulltext-preparation-v2/markdown/Pf53a5ee15eef.md"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Limitation",
        "id": "L1",
        "study_id": "S1",
        "part_id": null,
        "statement": "The rationale behind the children's EQ VAS scores was not explored, so the discrepancy between reported health profiles and VAS scores can only be explained speculatively.",
